Debian/Ubuntu packaging for the GEOS module
===========================================

qore-geos-module ships native GEOS and the GEOSDataProvider source/AOT module,
compiler metadata, provider resources and locale catalogs. The doc package
contains both API references and example tests. Debhelper generates matching
debug symbols for the native and compiled Qore modules.

Use an isolated native build environment with the packaged Qore runtime and
libqore-dev, then install debian/control's Build-Depends. Qualification targets
Ubuntu 26.04 amd64 with the Qore 3.0 SDK. Other releases and architectures need
matching SDKs and native tests. Cross builds fail explicitly because Qore tools
run during compilation. Use distribution GEOS (>= 3.12); newer optional APIs
are enabled according to its headers and checked by the upstream tests.
No bundled library or build-time network download is needed.

The runtime and libqore SONAME minimum versions come from the SDK used to
compile the module. dh_shlibdeps supplies the GEOS and other library versions
required by its imported symbols. The native runtime is not Multi-Arch: same.

Build and metadata rules
-------------------------

AOT is enabled, source-tree qmod symlinks are disabled and noopt selects AOT
optimization level zero. QCC_JOBS=1 fixes codegen partitioning independently
of CPU count and GNU make jobserver load; independent targets still compile
in parallel. Timezone and locale are fixed for reproducibility. Qore tools
use only this build and the packaged standard library, including metadata
extraction. Debian prefix maps also cover AOT compiler output.

The stripping wrapper copied from Qore preserves appended dependency and
source-location metadata; its real-ELF tests run during builds. dwz skips the
runtime because it does not support all LLVM DWARF forms. All catalogs and
the project ownership manifest are packaged; the complete standard-locale
check runs against the built provider, using qore-misc-tools.

Source preparation and qualification
------------------------------------

Use a fresh version for each changed upload. This snapshot precedes 1.0.0.
From a clean committed checkout:

    version=1.0.0~git20260928.1
    mkdir -p ../geos-package-work
    git archive --format=tar --prefix="qore-geos-module-$version/" \
        HEAD -- . ':!debian' | xz > \
        "../geos-package-work/qore-geos-module_$version.orig.tar.xz"
    tar -xf "../geos-package-work/qore-geos-module_$version.orig.tar.xz" \
        -C ../geos-package-work
    cp -a debian "../geos-package-work/qore-geos-module-$version/"
    cd "../geos-package-work/qore-geos-module-$version"
    dpkg-buildpackage -S -us -uc

Extract the .dsc into a fresh directory and run dpkg-buildpackage -b -us -uc
unprivileged with networking disabled. -B builds runtime/debug only; -A builds
documentation. nodoc in DEB_BUILD_OPTIONS suppresses HTML generation, and the
nodoc profile also omits the doc package. Do not use nocheck for the full
qualification build; subsequent profile/reproducibility builds may use it.

Run both upstream suites. Installed tests copy only test scripts into a
temporary directory, explicitly preload the installed AOT provider and use
no source checkout. They exercise geometry operations, serialization, spatial
indexes and WKT/WKB/GeoJSON provider factories. A fresh qcc executable checks
named arguments, distance, WKB round trip and provider discovery.

Check Lintian, hardening, matching debug symbols, AOT trailers, installed
catalog/resource parity, a runtime-only install without the SDK, docs/debug
coinstallation, dpkg -V, purge/reinstall and reproducibility across distinct
paths and parallel job counts. Retain hashes, dependency inventories and logs.
Testing-PPA publication is separate from approval for a final general release.
